<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- An attacker that sees a player's own ship take or drop a faction's cover blows that cover as it does for player 1
     (native_gate_player_groups, a session default: this patch ships with md/setup.xml's,
     tools/dev/native_gate_player_groups.xml).

     X4's disengage handler (aiscripts/interrupt.disengage.xml, part of every attack) hears the target change owner.
     For the ship the player flies, seen by the attacker, a change of the cover owner means the player put on or took off
     a disguise in sight of the enemy: the attacker signals LoseCover to that ship (md/cover.xml takes it from the group
     of the players' ships) and keeps attacking. Any other target gets its relation boost reset, and the attack stops
     when the new owner may not be attacked. The script is the attacker's and runs outside every player's scope, where
     `player` is player 1, so a player 2..N in disguise could drop an attacker by putting the cover on. Here the ship any
     player controls is also "the ship the player flies" ($X4LAN_Pilots on every player's entity, kept by the player
     groups at the same ticks on every client). Player 1's ship passes by the stock clause; without the gate nothing sets
     the table and the line is the stock one. Our own clause only; the stock script is patched in memory by X4's own diff
     loading, never on disk. -->
<diff>
 <replace sel="//do_if[@value='$target == player.occupiedship and this.assignedcontrolled.cansee.{$target}']/@value">($target == player.occupiedship or @player.entity.$X4LAN_Pilots.{$target}) and this.assignedcontrolled.cansee.{$target}</replace>
</diff>
